[
  {"id":1,"question":"The hallmark of Primary Health Care, without which Primary Health Care will not succeed is","options":["A. Community mobilization","B. Community participation","C. Self-reliance","D. Community motivation"],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":2,"question":"The following are attributes of Traditional Birth Attendants EXCEPT","options":["A. They are midwives who have limited training to acquire the skill of 'taking delivery' of a baby and are licensed to operate a 'maternity home'.","B. Mobilize women and children for maternal and child health clinics and encourage women to seek prenatal care.","C. Take careful history and physical examination of pregnant woman and identify those at risk for referral.","D. Health educate mothers on good nutrition and breast feeding."],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":3,"question":"The following methods can be used in carrying out community diagnosis EXCEPT","options":["A. Direct physical observation that is, on the spot assessment.","B. Obtaining record from the health centers.","C. Obtaining information by the use of questionnaire.","D. Use of advance computer technology to obtain information."],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":4,"question":"One of the following statements is NOT true of the rationale and role of community mobilization.","options":["A. It makes the community members to be aware and identify their own health problems and related health needs.","B. It makes the government to shy away from their total commitments and responsibilities thereby conserving their financial expenditure.","C. It allows individual community members to become involved in finding/planning solutions to their identified health problems.","D. Ensure consumer participation in Primary Health Care especially in the area of provision of fund, infrastructures etc."],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":5,"question":"According to World Health Organization (WHO) guideline on the quality of a safe portable during water, water is considered unsafe if the presence of coliform/pyrogen is greater than","options":["A. 5/100 mls.","B. 10/100 mls.","C. 15/100 mls.","D. 20/100 mls."],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":6,"question":"The act of taking a life to relieve suffering is known as","options":["A. Eutanasia.","B. Euthernasia.","C. Euthanasia.","D. Buthanazia."],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":7,"question":"Nosocomial /Hospital acquired infections are those that occurred when","options":["A. The incubation period and the manifestations of the disease is shorter than the period of Patients Hospitalization.","B. The incubation period and the manifestations of the disease is longer than the period of Patients hospitalization.","C. The incubation period and the manifestation of the disease are the same.","D. The incubation period and the manifestation of the disease are immediately."],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":8,"question":"Need for food, air, elimination, rest etc are classified under which of the following Abraham Maslow's hierarchy of needs","options":["A. Self-actualization.","B. Love and belonging.","C. Safety need.","D. Physiological needs."],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":9,"question":"Hindrances to the successful eradication of poliomyelitis in Nigeria could be attributed following factors EXCEPT","options":["A. Beliefs and taboos.","B. Inaccurate dosage of the vaccine given.","C. Shortage of funds and logistics to support immunization programme.","D. Maintenance of cold chain system."],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":10,"question":"The first modern pharmacological compound was made by","options":["A. Friedrick Wohler.","B. Hippocrates.","C. Florence Nightingale.","D. Edward Jenner."],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":11,"question":"The combination of drug that interacts with another to produce increased activity which is than the sum of the effects of the two drugs given separately is called","options":["A. Synergism.","B. Summation.","C. Addition.","D. Combined therapy."],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":12,"question":"The capacity of a drug to produce the maximum desired effect is referred to as","options":["A. Drug efficacy.","B. Dosage efficacy.","C. Pharmacological efficacy.","D. Therapeutic efficacy."],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":13,"question":"An unusual exaggerated reaction to drug is called","options":["A. Intolerance.","B. Hyper toxicity.","C. Side effect.","D. Idiosyncrasy."],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":14,"question":"A condition associated with repeated administration of a drug harmful to the individual and sometimes to the society is known as","options":["A. Drug repetition","B. Drug dependence","C. Drug reliance","D. Drug hazards"],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":15,"question":"When diary products like milk are taken with antibiotics like tetracycline","options":["A. There is decreased absorption of the drug in the stomach.","B. There is increased absorption of the drug in the stomach.","C. The potency of the drug is increased.","D. The potency of the drug is decreased."],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":16,"question":"In a client with alcoholism, the primary rehabilitator is the","options":["A. Nurse.","B. Entire health care team.","C. The family.","D. The Physician."],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":17,"question":"The criteria for providing the causal relationship between a Micro-Organism and a specific disease is known as","options":["A. Leeuwenhoek postulate.","B. Pasteur's postulate.","C. Koch's postulate.","D. Jenner's postulate."],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":18,"question":"The ability of the body's cells to engulf foreign materials such as Micro-Organisms is called","options":["A. Body defence.","B. Specific defence.","C. Phagocytosis.","D. Cell defence."],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":19,"question":"The first direct demonstration of the role of bacteria in causing disease came from the study of anthrax by","options":["A. Fidel Castro.","B. Robert Koch.","C. Edward Jenner.","D. Louis Pasteur."],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":20,"question":"Oxytetracyclin and chlortetracycline are naturally produced by ........specie of Micro-Organisms.","options":["A. Actinomyce.","B. Clostridium.","C. Baccitus.","D. Pseudomonas."],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":21,"question":"The process of inhibiting the growth and multiplication of Micro-Organism is called","options":["A. Bacteriostatic.","B. Phagocytosis.","C. Bacteriocidal,","D. Disinfection."],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":22,"question":"Psychoanalytic theory in the area of child psychology was propounded by","options":["A. Eric Erickson","B. Karl Menninger","C. Sigmoid Freud","D. Melanie Klein"],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":23,"question":"The following are components of Psychology EXCEPT","options":["A. Stratification.","B. Emotions.","C. Motivations.","D. Personality."],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":24,"question":"One of the following is NOT a coping mechanism","options":["A. Problem-focused coping mechanism.","B. Cognitive-focused coping mechanism.","C. Emotion-focused coping mechanism.","D. Solution-focused coping mechanism."],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":25,"question":"The term which describe a therapeutic process based on the belief that behavioural disorders are related to unresolved anxiety provoking childhood experiences that are repressed into the unconscious is known as","options":["A. Socioanalysis.","B. Physioanalysis.","C. Psychoanalysis.","D. Repressed analysis."],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":26,"question":"The following are characteristics of Personality disorders EXCEPT","options":["A. Relatively persistent traits.","B. Spontaneous exacerbations and remissions.","C. Resistance to treatment.","D. Results in dementia."],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":27,"question":"Hyperaldosteronism occurs due to damage to the","options":["A. Adrenal gland","B. Suprarenal gland","C. Renal gland","D. Pituitary gland"],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":28,"question":"The test that best evaluate the ability of the kidneys to regulate fluid is","options":["A. Blood urea Nitrogen (BUN)","B. Urine specific gravity","C. Creatinine","D. Urinary protein test"],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":29,"question":"The increase in the percentage of Eosinophils leads to","options":["A. Excitement","B. Allergic reactions","C. Confusion","D. Disorientation"],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":30,"question":"The following are functions of plasma protein EXCEPT","options":["A. Transportation","B. Buffering effect.","C. Osmotic pressure","D. Antibiotic effect."],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":31,"question":"The ABC of Cardio Pulmonary Resuscitation (CPR) mean","options":["A. Artificial, breathing, compression.","B. Always be careful","C. Airway, breathing, consciousness.","D. Airways, breathing, circulation"],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":32,"question":"The state of being free from Micro-Organisms is known as","options":["A. Asepsis.","B. Antiseptic.","C. Aseptic technique.","D. Sterilization"],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":33,"question":"The position in which the patient lies on his back with two or three pillows under his head is known as","options":["A. Recumbent position.","B. Dorsal position.","C. Prone position.","D. Semi-recumbent position."],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":34,"question":"The following are adaptive processes of the cell EXCEPT","options":["A. Hypertrophy.","B. Hyperplasia.","C. Atrophy.","D. Lysis."],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":35,"question":"Contractures often occur after burns healing due to","options":["A. Secondary infection.","B. Excess fibrous tissue formation.","C. Lack of adequate blood supply.","D. Weakness of connective tissue."],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":36,"question":"Which of these surgical procedures involves removal of a body organ","options":["A. Mammoplasty.","B. Colostomy.","C. Cholecystectomy.","D. Herniorraphy."],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":37,"question":"The third, fourth and sixth cranial nerves control the","options":["A. Pupil size.","B. Visual field.","C. Extraocular movement.","D. Intraocular movement."],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":38,"question":"The purpose of tonometry is to determine","options":["A. Intraocular pressure.","B. Corneal curvature.","C. Sensitivity of the cornea.","D. Refractive error."],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":39,"question":"The characteristics of serous otitis media include","options":["A. Retracted ear drum.","B. Perforated ear drum.","C. Purulent drainage from the ear.","D. Dilation of eustachian tube."],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":40,"question":"When a hernia can be pushed back into the abdominal cavity, it is called","options":["A. Incarcerated.","B. Irreducible.","C. Reducible.","D. Strangulated."],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":41,"question":"In acute pancreatitis, the most specific pathophysiology is","options":["A. Auto digestion.","B. Overproduction of enzyme.","C. Lack of secretion of enzymes.","D. Cellular disorganization."],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":42,"question":"The clinical manifestation of acute pyelonephritis include","options":["A. Hematuria and hemoptysis.","B. Elevated blood pressure.","C. Albuminuria and oedema.","D. Vomiting, headache and malaise."],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":43,"question":"The blood vessels that have the primary function of transporting nutrients and metabolites are known as","options":["A. Capillaries.","B. Arteries.","C. Venules.","D. Arterioles."],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":44,"question":"The most common problem associated with immunosuppressive therapy is","options":["A. Hyper coagulation.","B. Anaemia.","C. Thrombocytopenia.","D. Predisposition to infection."],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":45,"question":"The following are characteristics of the Pancreas EXCEPT","options":["A. It weighs between 60-90g.","B. It has both the exocrine and endocrine functions.","C. Contains cells called islets of Langerhans.","D. The alpha cells secrete insulin."],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":46,"question":"In Acromegaly, the following features will be present EXCEPT","options":["A. Facial changes.","B. Enlargement of extremities.","C. Emotional disturbances.","D. Abdominal enlargement."],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":47,"question":"Which of the following substances are necessary for converting prothrombin to thrombin?","options":["A. Thromboplastic and calcium.","B. Fibrinogen and calcium.","C. Fibrin and thromboplastic.","D. Platelet set factor and calcium."],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":48,"question":"A normocytic, normochromic anaemia may be caused by","options":["A. Chronic infection.","B. Bone marrow suppression.","C. Folic acid deficiency.","D. Vitamin B deficiency."],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":49,"question":"The primary emphasis in the dietary management of congestive cardiac failure is","options":["A. Increased fluid intake.","B. Reduction in dietary potassium.","C. Reduced dietary sodium.","D. Low cholesterol and low saturated fat diet."],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":50,"question":"the term that describes the body's ability to maintain its normal state is","options":["A. Homeostasis.","B. Tolerance.","C. Metabolism.","D. Catabolism."],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":51,"question":"The most common preventable complication of abdominal surgery is","options":["A. Atelectasis.","B. Thrombophlebitis.","C. Urinary retention.","D. Pulmonary oedema."],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":52,"question":"The following are pre renal causes of acute renal failure EXCEPT","options":["A. Haemorrhage.","B. Urinary tract obstruction.","C. Myocardial infarction.","D. Sepsis."],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":53,"question":"The first clinical manifestation of incompatible blood transfusion is","options":["A. Hypotension and bradycardia.","B. Anuria and loin pain.","C. Pyrexia and skin rashes.","D. Haemorrhage under the skin."],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":54,"question":"False sensory perception in the absence of real external stimuli is called","options":["A. Delusion.","B. Hallucination.","C. Dejavu.","D. Illusion."],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":55,"question":"A client tells the Nurse that his body is made of wood and is quiet heavy. This is a clinical manifestation of one of the following:","options":["A. Compulsion.","B. Autism.","C. Depersonalization.","D. Obsession."],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":56,"question":"The priority nursing assessment for a client with cerebrovascular accident within the first 24 hours of admission is","options":["A. Pupil size and papillary response.","B. Cholesterol level.","C. Echocardiogram.","D. Bowel sounds."],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":57,"question":"The fluid shift in a client with burns injury results from increase in the","options":["A. Total volume of circulating whole blood.","B. Total volume of intravascular plasma.","C. Permeability of capillary wall.","D. Permeability of kidney tubules."],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":58,"question":"The main goal of treatment in acute glomerulonephritis is to","options":["A. Encourage activity.","B. Encourage high protein intake.","C. Maintain fluid balance.","D. Teach intermittent urinary catheterization."],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":59,"question":"The first step in applying the quality improvement process to an activity is to","options":["A. Assemble a team to review and revise the activity.","B. Collect data to measure the status of activity.","C. Select an activity for improvement.","D. Set a measurable standard for the activity."],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":60,"question":"Passive range of motion exercises prevent","options":["A. Contractures.","B. Osteoporosis.","C. Muscle atrophy.","D. Fractures."],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":61,"question":"Principle of good body mechanics includes","options":["A. Keeping knees in locked position.","B. Maintaining a wide-base of support.","C. Bending at the waist to maintain centres of gravity.","D. Holding objects away from the body for better leverage."],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":62,"question":"When performing a breast self-assessment, a female patient is taught to palpate the upper outer quadrant of the breast tissue because this area is:","options":["A. Where the breast lumps are often located.","B. Where the most lymphnodes are located.","C. More prone to calcification.","D. Where small lumps are found."],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":63,"question":"When assessing the patient for range of joint movement, the patient is asked to move the arm away from the body. This evaluates movement of","options":["A. Flexion.","B. Extension.","C. Abduction.","D. Adduction."],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":64,"question":"Poor oxygenation of the blood affects the pulse rate and causes it to become","options":["A. Bounding.","B. Irregular.","C. Tachycardiac.","D. Bradycardiac."],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":65,"question":"The following are skin traction devices EXCEPT","options":["A. Balanced suspension traction.","B. Gallows traction.","C. Dunlop's traction.","D. Bucks extension traction."],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":66,"question":"The premature destruction of erythrocyte occurring at a rate that bone marrow cannot compensate is called","options":["A. Haemolytic anaemia.","B. Aplastic anaemia.","C. Pernicious anaemia.","D. Iron deficiency anaemia."],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":67,"question":"Grave's disease is another name for","options":["A. Hypothyroidism.","B. Hyperthyroidism.","C. Cushing's syndrome.","D. Hyperaldosteroidism."],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":68,"question":"Dilatation of the renal pelvis and calyx with collection of urine is referred to as","options":["A. Nephrotic syndrome.","B. Pyelonephritis.","C. Pyelonephritis.","D. Hydronephrosis."],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":69,"question":"The incubation period of Hepatitis B is","options":["A. 50 - 180 days.","B. 50 - 160 days.","C. 50 - 170 days.","D. 50 -- 190 days."],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":70,"question":"The volume of air in vital capacity is","options":["A. 3000 mls.","B. 4000 mls.","C. 4700 mls.","D. 8000 mls."],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":71,"question":"The percentage (%) of oxygen in atmospheric air is","options":["A. 18%","B. 20%","C. 21%","D. 23%"],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":72,"question":"The Pituitary gland lies in the","options":["A. Stella--tunica of the sphenoid bone.","B. Stella-tunica of the frontal bone.","C. Stella-tunica of the ethmoid bone.","D. Stella-tunica of the occipital bone."],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":73,"question":"The Autoclave is the instrument of choice for","options":["A. Sterilization.","B. Disinfectant.","C. Radiation.","D. Fumigation."],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":74,"question":"One of the major functions of fat in the body is to","options":["A. Build the muscles.","B. Repair body tissues.","C. Produce heat and energy.","D. Replace damaged cells."],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":75,"question":"The thermometer standard scales most commonly used","options":["A. Centigrade and Fahrenheit.","B. Fahrenheit and centimeter.","C. Centigrade and Fahrenheit.","D. Centimeter and centigrade."],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":76,"question":"Rigor is defined as","options":["A. Sudden but steady increase in pulse rate.","B. Shivering effect of fever.","C. Sudden severe shivering attack.","D. Gradual shivering attack."],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":77,"question":"C.D.A. denotes","options":["A. Controlled Dangerous Act.","B. Controlled Drugs Act.","C. Controlled Drugs Actions.","D. Controlled Disease Act."],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":78,"question":"A state of complete unconsciousness when the person's eyes are wide open is called","options":["A. Coma vigil.","B. Night vigil.","C. Eye vigil.","D. Open coma."],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":79,"question":"The following are components of school health services EXCEPT","options":["A. Environmental sanitation.","B. Dental health services.","C. Mental health services.","D. Immunization."],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":80,"question":"The following are locations for the administration of subcutaneous injections EXCEPT","options":["A. Abdomen.","B. Lower hips.","C. Upper back.","D. Lateral thighs."],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":81,"question":"The following are the classifications of intravenous solutions used for fluid replacement EXCEPT","options":["A. Crystalloids.","B. Colloids.","C. Blood and blood products.","D. Electrolytes."],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":82,"question":"The theory which views the client adaptive system was propounded by.","options":["A. Florence Nightingale.","B. Virginia Henderson.","C. Dorothy Orem.","D. Sister Calesta Roy."],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":83,"question":"The difference between the systolic and diastolic blood pressure is called","options":["A. Pulse pressure.","B. Intermittent pressure.","C. Intermediate pressure.","D. Pulse system."],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":84,"question":"The replacement of destroyed cells by cells that are identical in structure and function is called","options":["A. Reactivation.","B. New growth.","C. Regeneration.","D. Degeneration."],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":85,"question":"Another name for the antibody-mediated defence is","options":["A. Humoral immunity.","B. Humonal immunity.","C. Active immunity.","D. Herd immunity."],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":86,"question":"Keratosis caused by friction and pressure from shoe is known as","options":["A. Corn.","B. Callus.","C. warts.","D. Fissures."],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":87,"question":"A visible, hard deposit of plague and dead bacteria that forms on the gum line is called","options":["A. Tartar.","B. Plague.","C. Pyorrhea's.","D. Gingivitis."],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":88,"question":"In congenital cyanotic heart disease, cyanosis occurs when there is more than ..........circulating deoxygenated haemoglobin.","options":["A. 4g/dl.","B. 5g/dl.","C. 6g/dl.","D. 7g/dl."],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":89,"question":"One of the following is NOT an obstructive lesion of the heart","options":["A. Coarctation of the aorta. Pulmonary stenosis.","B. Aortic stenosis.","C. Tetraology of fallot.","D. None"],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":90,"question":"A lesion with membranous sac containing cerebrospinal fluid and neural tissue is referred to as","options":["A. Spinal bifida.","B. Meningomyelocele.","C. Meningocele.","D. Spinal bifida occulta."],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":91,"question":"Primary dysmenorrhea occurs most commonly due to","options":["A. Elevated level of estrogen.","B. Elevated level of uterine prostaglandins.","C. Endometrosis.","D. Uterine myoma."],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":92,"question":"The normal flora in the squamous epithelial lining of the vagina is","options":["A. Lactovirus.","B. Lactobacilli.","C. Glycol bacilli.","D. Glycol fungi."],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":93,"question":"The following are the ligaments that support the uterus EXCEPT","options":["A. Transverse cervical ligament.","B. Broad ligament.","C. Uterosacral ligament.","D. Round ligament."],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":94,"question":"The act in which there is a threat or attempt to do bodily harm is called","options":["A. Assault.","B. Battery.","C. Tort.","D. Crime."],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":95,"question":"A good organizational objective should have the following characteristics EXCEPT","options":["A. Flexibility.","B. Realistic.","C. Consistent.","D. Time frame."],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":96,"question":"The father of scientific management is","options":["A. Fredrick Taylor.","B. Henry Fayol.","C. Max Weber.","D. Henry Gantt."],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":97,"question":"The process of grouping similar jobs together and putting then into units is called","options":["A. Departmentalization.","B. Unitary.","C. Groups.","D. Differentiation."],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":98,"question":"The compact ball of capillaries in the nephron is called","options":["A. The nephron loop","B. The glomerulus","C. The renal corpuscle","D. The vasa recta"],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":99,"question":"For description purposes, the pharynx is divided into","options":["A. Two parts","B. Three parts","C. Four parts","D. Five parts"],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":100,"question":"The body attempt to maintain a stable internal environment by achieving balance in a process known as","options":["A. Hematemesis","B. Haemoptysis","C. Homeostasis","D. Haemolysis"],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":101,"question":"Electrolytes are particularly important in the body in the following ways EXCEPT","options":["A. As essential minerals","B. In the control of osmosis","C. To maintain acid-base balance","D. For deamination"],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":102,"question":"The volume of air left in the lungs after maximum exhalation is called","options":["A. Total lung volume","B. Vital lung volume","C. Tidal volume","D. Residual volume"],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":103,"question":"The following are the planes of the body EXCEPT","options":["A. Sagittal plane","B. Transverse plane","C. Frontal plane","D. Bilateral plane"],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":104,"question":"The respiratory system assists in gas exchange and performs the following functions EXCEPT","options":["A. Regulation of body pH","B. Olfaction","C. Voice production","D. Induction"],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":105,"question":"The hair on a six (6) year old child's arm is termed","options":["A. Vellus","B. Lanugo","C. Terminal hair","D. Alopecia"],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":106,"question":"An inherited condition or disease characterized by severe anaemia due to an abnormal form of haemoglobin in the blood is called","options":["A. Down's syndrome","B. Thalassemia","C. Chromosomal defect","D. Turner Syndrome"],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":107,"question":"A condition in which part of the stomach protrudes into the chest through the opening in the diaphragm that is normally occupied by the oesophagus is known as","options":["A. Inguinal hernia","B. Hiatus hernia","C. Strangulated hernia","D. Obstructed hernia"],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":108,"question":"A common defect in the stomach of infants in which the pyloric sphincter is greatly thickened resulting in interference with normal stomach emptying is called","options":["A. Peptic ulcer","B. Oesophageal fistula","C. Hypertrophic pyloric stenosis","D. Gastritis"],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":109,"question":"A congenital abnormality in the heart in which there is a hole in the dividing wall between the left and right sides of the heart is called","options":["A. Stenosis","B. Patent ductus arteriosus","C. Septal defect","D. Incompetent heart valve"],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":110,"question":"Which of the following is the pressure at which a korotkoff sound is first heard when cuff pressure decreases and is no longer able to keep the brachial artery closed during systole?","options":["A. Pulse pressure","B. Systolic pressure","C. Diastolic pressure","D. Blood pressure"],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":111,"question":"The 3rd, 4th and 6th cranial nerves controls","options":["A. Pupil size","B. Visual field","C. Extraocular movement","D. Intraocular movement"],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":112,"question":"The following are major processes essential for urine formation EXCEPT","options":["A. Filtration","B. Separation","C. Tubular reabsorption","D. Tubular secretion"],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":113,"question":"The movement of materials across the filtration membrane into the Bowman's capsule is called","options":["A. Reabsorption","B. Secretion","C. Filtration","D. Absorption"],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":114,"question":"An inflammation of the renal pelvis, medulla or cortex that often begins as a bacterial infection of the renal pelvis and then extends to the kidney is called","options":["A. Pyelonephritis","B. Glomerulonephritis","C. Nephritis","D. Pyelitis"],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":115,"question":"The chemical called Tar in a cigarette is responsible for in smokers.","options":["A. Asthma","B. Dizziness","C. Cancer","D. Addiction"],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":116,"question":"The agent commonly responsible for pneumonia in children under age five (5) is","options":["A. Fungi","B. Bacteria","C. Viruses","D. Mycoplasma"],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":117,"question":"The history of smoking, cough and dyspnoea accompanied by abnormal and permanent enlargement of the alveoli is suggestive of","options":["A. Asthma","B. Chronic bronchitis","C. Obstructive sleep apnea","D. Emphysema"],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":118,"question":"The surgical creation of an opening into the jejunum for the purpose of administering fluids, nutrition formula and medications is called","options":["A. Jejunoscopy","B. Jejunostomy","C. Gastrojejunostomy","D. Gastrojejunoscopy"],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":119,"question":"An artificial opening created between body cavity and the body surface is known as","options":["A. Stomata","B. Tracheostomy","C. Stoma","D. Fistula"],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":120,"question":"Which of the following strategies may NOT help prevent some of the uncomfortable signs and symptoms of dumping syndrome related to tube feeding?","options":["A. Slow the formula instillation rate","B. Administer feeding at room temperature","C. Administer feeding by continuous drip rather than by bolus","D. Advice patient to remain in Fowlers' position for one hour after feeding"],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":121,"question":"While educating a patient undergoing a neck dissection, the nurse emphasized on the possibility of developing the following complications EXCEPT","options":["A. Haemorrhage","B. Chyle fistula","C. Nerve injury","D. Infection"],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":122,"question":"A patient with an inflamed gall bladder experiences pain after eating due to contraction of the gall bladder. The mechanism responsible for this action is","options":["A. Production of secretions in the duodenum","B. Production of cholecystokinin by the duodenum","C. Release of gastrin from the stomach antrum","D. Production of bile by the liver"],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":123,"question":"The following are common causes of hemoptysis EXCEPT","options":["A. Pulmonary infection","B. Carcinoma of the lung","C. Foreign body","D. Abnormality of the blood vessels"],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":124,"question":"The following are accessory muscles of respiration EXCEPT","options":["A. Sternocleidomastoid","B. Scalene","C. Internal intercostal","D. External intercostal"],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":125,"question":"Hypercapnic respiratory failure is most likely to occur in patients who have","options":["A. Large airway permissiveness as a result of bronchodilator","B. Slow, shallow respiration as a result of sedative overdose","C. Well, vascularized area of lungs","D. Rapid, deep respiration in response to pneumonia"],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":126,"question":"The secondary pacemaker of the heart located in the right atrial wall near the tricuspid valve is called","options":["A. Sino-atrial node","B. Apical impulse","C. Baroreceptors","D. Atrioventricular (AV) node"],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":127,"question":"The difference between the systolic and the diastolic pressure is called","options":["A. Blood pressure","B. Pulse pressure","C. Pulse rhythm","D. Pulse contour"],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":128,"question":"The vibration usually felt when palpating the patient's popliteal pulse is referred to as","options":["A. Threading knee pulse","B. Bruit at the artery site","C. Bounding pulse volume","D. Trill of the popliteal artery"],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":129,"question":"The most abundant intracellular ion in the human body is","options":["A. Sodium","B. Calcium","C. Potassium","D. Magnesium"],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":130,"question":"The transmission of maternal antibodies to the foetus in utero and through breast feeding is considered as","options":["A. Natural active immunization","B. Natural passive immunization","C. Artificial active immunization","D. Artificial passive immunization"],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":131,"question":"The following makes the pentavalent vaccine EXCEPT","options":["A. Hepatitis B","B. Haemophilus Influenza Type B","C. Whooping cough","D. Tuberculosis"],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":132,"question":"The following are cold chain equipment used to ensure that vaccines remain within acceptable temperatures EXCEPT","options":["A. Temperature chart","B. Vaccine carrier","C. Vaccine vial monitor","D. Vaccine cold chain"],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":133,"question":"The need for food, air, elimination, rest e.t.c are classified under Maslow's hierarchy of needs.","options":["A. Self-actualization","B. Love and belonging","C. Safety need","D. Physiological need"],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":134,"question":"The following are strategies developed to meet immunization demand EXCEPT","options":["A. Make vaccines cheap","B. Disease surveillance","C. Community motivation","D. Special immunization campaigns"],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":135,"question":"Which of the following is NOT an indication for drug adverse reaction surveillance?","options":["A. Detect, report and respond to adverse event following immunizations timely and promptly","B. Ensure that coincidental events are not falsely blamed on vaccination","C. Collect data about injection safety","D. Maintain confidence of the community and health workers in the immunization programme by properly and promptly responding to their concern"],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":136,"question":"The following are adverse events classifications in immunization EXCEPT","options":["A. Vaccine reaction","B. Vaccine sublimation","C. Vaccine error","D. Programme error"],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":137,"question":"To understand the principles of disease control, it is essential to understand the relationship between","options":["A. Agent, host and environment","B. Instrument, host and environment","C. Instrument, microorganism and environment","D. Agent, microorganism and host"],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":138,"question":"Essential drugs are those that satisfy the priority health care needs of majority of the population. These drugs are selected based on the following criteria EXCEPT","options":["A. Disease prevalence and public health relevance","B. Preference of the community leader","C. Evidence of clinical efficacy and safety","D. Comparative cost effectiveness"],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":139,"question":"The following are main functions of the teeth EXCEPT","options":["A. Protection","B. Mastication","C. Speech","D. Aesthetics"],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":140,"question":"The act of taking a life to relieve suffering is known as","options":["A. Euthanasia","B. Luftanasia","C. Euthanasea","D. Euthanazia"],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":141,"question":"The two main approaches to primary health care are","options":["A. Intersectoral and multidisciplinary approaches","B. Intrasectoral and multidisciplinary approaches","C. Collaborative and intersectoral approaches","D. Intersectoral and multisectoral approaches"],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":142,"question":"The following are components of health belief model EXCEPT","options":["A. Perceived susceptibility to a disease","B. Perceived causes of a disease","C. Perceived seriousness of a disease","D. Perceived value of action"],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":143,"question":"The following are principles of ethics EXCEPT","options":["A. Justice","B. Beneficence","C. Autonomy","D. Consent"],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":144,"question":"The intentional touching of another person's body without consent is termed","options":["A. Assault","B. Battery","C. Invasion of privacy","D. Defamation of character"],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":145,"question":"The following are responsibilities of the nurse when admitting a patient into the hospital or health care facility EXCEPT","options":["A. Meeting all the needs of the patient","B. Introduction and orientation","C. Baseline assessment","D. Care of belongings"],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":146,"question":"The criteria for providing the causal relationship between a microorganism and a specific disease is called","options":["A. Laeuwenhoek postulate","B. Pasteurs's postulate","C. Koch's postulate","D. Jenner's postulate"],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":147,"question":"In documentation and report writing, the nurse is expected to do the following EXCEPT","options":["A. Record a change in clients condition and show that follow up action were taken","B. Read the nurses' notes prior to care to determine if there has been a change in the client condition","C. Leave a blank space for a colleague to record/chart later","D. Record the client response to interventions"],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":148,"question":"The average adult dose of paracetamol is 600mg. What is the appropriate dose of this medication for an 8 year old child?","options":["A. 110mg","B. 120mg","C. 130mg","D. 140mg"],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":149,"question":"Increase in progesterone during ovulation can cause a woman's body temperature to increase by","options":["A. 0.5°F - 1°F","B. 1°F - 2°F","C. 1.5°F - 2°F","D. 2.5°F - 3°F"],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":150,"question":"The amount of blood ejected with each ventricular contraction is called","options":["A. Cardiac volume","B. Ventricular volume","C. Stroke volume","D. Pulse volume"],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":151,"question":"The body mass index (BMI) of a 25-year old man weighing 9lkg, height of 165cm falls in the category of","options":["A. Underweight","B. Normal weight","C. Over weight","D. Obese"],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":152,"question":"The following are steps in the process of evaluation EXCEPT","options":["A. Review the goals or predicted outcomes","B. Focuses on the manner in which care is given","C. Collect data about the client responses to nursing action","D. Relate nursing plans to client outcomes"],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":153,"question":"The commonest anatomical site recommended for intramuscular injections in adult is","options":["A. Deltoid muscles","B. Rectus femoris muscles","C. Ventrogluteal muscles","D. Dorsogluteal muscles"],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":154,"question":"The best position to put a conscious patient that required promotion of lung expansion is","options":["A. Fowlers' position","B. Semi Fowlers' position","C. Trendelenburg position","D. Reverse Trendelenburg position"],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":155,"question":"The position used to promote breathing when the bed is raised to an angle of 30° is called","options":["A. Cardiac position","B. Fowlers' position","C. Semi Fowlers' position","D. Recumbent position"],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":156,"question":"Which of the following is wrong about patient's position during blood pressure measurements?","options":["A. Blood pressure measurements in pregnant patients should be taken with them sitting or lying on their side at a 450 angle","B. All patients should be reminded not to have their legs crossed if seated","C. The patient's arm should be supported in a horizontal position at mid-sternum level","D. The patient's arm should be supported in a horizontal position"],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":157,"question":"The following are factors that affects elimination pattern of an individual EXCEPT","options":["A. Emotional stress","B. High carbohydrate and fat diet","C. Use of narcotics and antibiotics","D. High fibre diet"],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":158,"question":"The following are classification of enemas EXCEPT","options":["A. Medicated enemas","B. Nutritive enemas","C. Anthelminthic enemas","D. Hydrative enemas"],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":159,"question":"In the management of biomedical waste, the nurse should do the following EXCEPT","options":["A. Chemically treat incinerable waste","B. Mutilate disposable item such as gloves","C. Disinfect the waste so that it is no longer the source of pathogenic organism","D. Ensure that the wastes are chlorinated before disposal"],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":160,"question":"The most common method of protection from biomedical waste hazard and infection spread in the hospital is","options":["A. Hand washing","B. Protective clothing","C. Foot protection","D. Barrier nursing"],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":161,"question":"The following are broad categories of medical waste treatment technologies EXCEPT","options":["A. Mechanical process","B. Thermal process","C. Chemical process","D. Disinfection process"],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":162,"question":"Chemical digestion of carbohydrate begins with","options":["A. Pancreatic amylase","B. Salivary amylase","C. Maltase","D. Lactase"],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":163,"question":"The following are essential (indispensable) amino acids EXCEPT","options":["A. Histidine","B. Leucine","C. Alanine","D. Isoleucine"],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":164,"question":"Amino acids are absorbed through the mucosa of the small intestine by an active transport with the aid of","options":["A. Vitamin K","B. Vitamin B","C. Vitamin B6","D. Vitamin C"],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":165,"question":"In the digestion of protein, hydrochloric acid converts pepsinogen to an active enzyme called","options":["A. Trypsin","B. Chymotrypsin","C. Pepsin","D. Polypeptides"],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":166,"question":"The following are lipids EXCEPT","options":["A. Triglycerides","B. Phospholipids","C. Sterols","D. Pepsin"],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":167,"question":"About 95% of consumed fat is absorbed mostly in the","options":["A. Small and large intestine","B. Stomach and duodenum","C. Duodenum and jejunum","D. Stomach and jejunum"],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":168,"question":"During starvation or uncontrolled diabetes, when the carbohydrate intake is inadequate unavailable, the body meets energy needs by breaking fatty acids by a process called","options":["A. Metabolism","B. Anabolism","C. Catabolism","D. Fatabolism"],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":169,"question":"What happens when dairy products like milk are taken with tetracycline?","options":["A. There is decreased absorption of the drug in the stomach","B. There is increased absorption of the drug in the stomach","C. The potency of the drug increased","D. The potency of the drug is decreased"],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":170,"question":"Which of the following is a major antioxidant?","options":["A. Vitamin A","B. Vitamin B","C. Vitamin C","D. Vitamin D"],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":171,"question":"Deficiency of Vitamin B leads to","options":["A. Beriberi","B. Pellagra","C. Rickets","D. Scurvy"],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":172,"question":"The minerals found in body fluids and tissues accounts for.......of the total body weight","options":["A. 4%","B. 10%","C. 15%","D. 209%"],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":173,"question":"The most effective therapy for client with bulimia is","options":["A. Nutritional education and dietary guidance","B. Nutritional counselling","C. Nutritional therapy","D. Nutritional monitoring and guidance"],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":174,"question":"Any preventable adverse drug event involving inappropriate medication use by a patient or health care professionals which may or may not cause harm is called","options":["A. Adverse drug reaction","B. Medication error","C. Drug overdose","D. Drug misuse"],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":175,"question":"The term used to quantify the extent of drug absorption is referred to as","options":["A. Bioavailability","B. Dissolution","C. Absorption","D. Distribution"],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":176,"question":"The process whereby drugs interact chemically and physiologically is termed","options":["A. Pharmacology","B. Pharmacokinetics","C. Pharmacodynamics","D. Pharmacognosy"],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":177,"question":"The following are important anatomical structures to be avoided while administering intramuscular injection at the dorsogluteal site EXCEPT","options":["A. Superior gluteal nerve","B. Sciatic nerve","C. Circumflex nerve","D. Superior gluteal artery"],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":178,"question":"Habitual, psychologic and physiologic dependence on a substance beyond normal voluntary control is known as","options":["A. Addiction","B. Tolerance","C. Dependence","D. Drug abuse"],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":179,"question":"The time it takes for one half of the original amount of a drug in the body to be removed from the body is known as","options":["A. Drug reduction","B. Drug hydrolysis","C. Half life","D. Drug life"],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":180,"question":"The following are implications for opening Drug Revolving Fund (DRF) EXCEPT","options":["A. The credibility of hospital services is enhanced if drugs are available at all times","B. There is a job satisfaction for hospital staff","C. There is decrease in self-medication and non-compliance","D. Government recurrent expenditure will be higher"],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":181,"question":"The following are adverse effects of beta-blockers on the cardiovascular system EXCEPT","options":["A. Tachycardia","B. Bradycardia","C. Hypotension","D. Heart failure"],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":182,"question":"First generation cephalosporins usually have active effect on","options":["A. Both gram positive and gram negative bacteria","B. Gram positive bacteria but limited activity against gram-negative bacteria","C. Gram-negative bacteria but limited activity against gram-positive bacteria","D. No effect on both gram-positive/negative bacteria"],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":183,"question":"The following are nursing diagnoses related to drug therapy EXCEPT","options":["A. Knowledge deficit related to drug therapy","B. Knowledge deficit about self-care","C. Risk for injury related to adverse effects of drugs","D. Fluid volume deficit related to drug action"],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":184,"question":"The process of enabling people to increase control on their health and its determinants and thereby improve their health is termed","options":["A. Health provision","B. Health prevention","C. Health evaluation","D. Health promotion"],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":185,"question":"The preventive measure that leads to early diagnosis and prompt treatment of a disease, illness or injury to prevent more severe problems from developing is termed","options":["A. Secondary prevention","B. Primary prevention","C. Tertiary prevention","D. Total prevention"],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":186,"question":"Periodic screening for high blood pressure and breast self-examination is a level of disease prevention","options":["A. Primary","B. Tertiary","C. Secondary","D. Continuous"],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":187,"question":"The community health nurse maintains a social and professional relationship with fellow nurses and other members of the health team. This is referred to as","options":["A. Inter and intra professional collaboration","B. Internal and external professional collaboration","C. Intra and inter professional collaboration","D. External and inter professional collaboration."],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":188,"question":"The family planning method that does not involve the use any drugs or devices is referred to as","options":["A. Hormone method","B. Artificial method","C. Natural method","D. Calendar method"],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":189,"question":"The following are harmful traditional practices EXCEPT","options":["A. Female genital mutilation","B. Male circumcision","C. Male child preference","D. Body scarification"],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":190,"question":"Vasectomy and tubal ligation are methods of","options":["A. Permanent and reversible contraception","B. Permanent and irreversible contraception","C. Permanent and long acting contraception","D. Permanent and protective contraception"],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":191,"question":"The physical factor within the environment that harm the musculoskeletal system is referred to as","options":["A. Biologic hazard","B. Chemical hazard","C. Ergonomic hazard","D. Physical hazard"],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":192,"question":"The study and analysis of the distribution pattern and determinants of health and disease condition in defined population is referred to as","options":["A. Incidence","B. Prevalence","C. Epidemiology","D. Parasitology"],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":193,"question":"The process of estimating and appraising the degree and dimension of students achievement is known as","options":["A. Evaluation","B. Test","C. Measurement","D. Continuous assessment"],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":194,"question":"The type of curriculum that covers all the aspects of human activity and development as well as cater for the individual and society is known as","options":["A. Subject centered curriculum","B. Societal curriculum","C. Basic education curriculum","D. Life centered curriculum"],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":195,"question":"The following are components of triangular processes of education EXCEPT","options":["A. Pupil","B. Parent","C. Teacher","D. Social environmental"],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":196,"question":"The document that communicates information about a specific course, defines expectations and responsibilities is known as","options":["A. Curriculum","B. Scheme of work","C. Lesson plan","D. Syllabus"],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":197,"question":"The change in behaviour as a result of experience is termed","options":["A. Teaching","B. Education","C. Maturation","D. Learning"],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":198,"question":"The main content of plasma is","options":["A. Nutrients","B. Oxygen","C. Water","D. Hormones"],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":199,"question":"A plane that divides the human body longitudinally into its anterior and posterior section is called","options":["A. Median plane","B. Transverse plane","C. Coronal plane","D. Trans-sectional plane"],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":200,"question":"Which of the following is a part of appendicular skeleton?","options":["A. Pelvic girdle","B. Skull","C. Vertebral column","D. Sternum"],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":201,"question":"The percentage of erythrocytes in the blood is","options":["A. 99%","B. 89%","C. 79%","D. 69%"],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":202,"question":"The tunica adventitia of arteries is made up of","options":["A. Muscle tissue","B. Squamous epithelium","C. Fibrous tissue","D. Columnar epithelium"],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":203,"question":"Which of the following situations can cause vasoconstriction?","options":["A. Hypoxia","B. Decreased temperature","C. Increased temperature","D. Increased secretion of cortisone"],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":204,"question":"The small mass of neuromuscular tissue that is situated in the wall of the atrial septum is","options":["A. Sino atrial node","B. Atrioventricular node","C. Bundle of His","D. Purkinje fibres"],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":205,"question":"The blood cell that is closely associated with allergy is","options":["A. Basophils","B. Monocytes","C. Lymphocytes","D. Eosinophils"],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":206,"question":"The pH range of saliva is","options":["A. 6.4- 8.5","B. 5.4- 7.5","C. 4.4 - 5.5","D. 3.4 -4.5"],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":207,"question":"The blood pH is kept between","options":["A. 9.35 and 9.45","B. 8.35 and 8.45","C. 7.35 and 7.45","D. 6.35 and 6.45"],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":208,"question":"In electrocardiography, the P-wave rises when","options":["A. Impulses spread from the AV node through the AV bundle","B. The ventricular muscles relax","C. The impulses from the SA node sweeps over the atria","D. Impulses are spread through the AV node to purkinje fibres"],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":209,"question":"Baroreceptors are located in the","options":["A. Wall of the aorta","B. Wall of the myocardium","C. Wall of the pulmonary artery","D. Wall of the endocardium"],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":210,"question":"The major contributor to the circulus arteriosus is","options":["A. External carotid artery","B. Internal carotid artery","C. Anterior communicating artery","D. Posterior communicating artery"],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":211,"question":"The full meaning of MALT in lymphatic system is","options":["A. Monocyte-Associated Lymphoid Tissue","B. Muscles-Associated Lymphoid Tissue","C. Monocyte-Activated Lymphoid Tissue","D. Mucosa-Associated Lymphoid Tissue"],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":212,"question":"Calcitonin is secreted in the","options":["A. Pituitary gland","B. Thyroid gland","C. Adrenal gland","D. Parathyroid gland"],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":213,"question":"Central chemoreceptors that stimulate the respiratory centre when arterial PCO2 rises is located in","options":["A. Medulla oblongata","B. Pons varoli","C. Cerebrum","D. Cerebellum"],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":214,"question":"Which of the following is the most common symptom of myocardial infarction?","options":["A. Chest pain","B. Dyspnea","C. Fatigue","D. Palpitation"],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":215,"question":"Complication of sinus bradycardia involves","options":["A. Hypertension","B. Decreased intracranial pressure","C. Hyperthyroidism","D. Myocarditis"],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":216,"question":"Which of the following assessment findings validate possible right hip fracture in an elderly client?","options":["A. The leg appears to be shortened, abducted and externally rotated","B. Planter flexion is observed with sciatic pain","C. The leg appears to be larger and externally rotated","D. Evidence of paresis with decreased sensation"],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":217,"question":"The most pertinent information in the diagnosis of cholecystitis is","options":["A. Flatulence","B. Nausea and vomiting","C. Right upper abdominal pain","D. Dyspepsia"],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":218,"question":"Which of the following is the cause of visual changes in a client diagnosed of Type 1 Diabetes mellitus?","options":["A. Bleeding into the inner ocular chamber of the eye","B. Gradual separation of the retina","C. Increase in size of the vessels","D. Gradual destruction and degeneration of the retina"],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":219,"question":"Which of the following statements is correct about Range Of Motion (ROM) exercise?","options":["A. Passive ROM exercise increase muscle strength","B. A full ROM exercise must be completed for the elderly","C. Exercise should be completed to the point of discomfort","D. ROM exercise assist the elderly to carry out activities of daily living"],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":220,"question":"Which of the following indicates severe allergic reaction to blood transfusion?","options":["A. Bounding peripheral pulse","B. Respiratory wheezing","C. Lower back pain","D. Chills"],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":221,"question":"Why is glucose monitoring preferred over urine testing for glucose in the elderly?","options":["A. The renal threshold for glucose is elevated in elderly","B. It is easier and less costly","C. Urine testing provides false negative result","D. Determination of the colour on a reagent strip varies from person to person"],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":222,"question":"Which type of food does the nurse encourage the client diagnosed with hypothyroidism to take?","options":["A. Food high in phosphorus","B. Food high in calcium","C. Food low in sodium","D. Food low in potassium"],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":223,"question":"Which of the following dietary changes is important for a child in the early stage of nephrotic syndrome?","options":["A. Adequate protein, low sodium intake","B. Low protein, low potassium intake","C. Low potassium, low calorie intake","D. Limited protein, high carbohydrate"],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":224,"question":"What is the priority nursing action for an elderly client with a body mass index (BMI) of 16?","options":["A. Document the client's BMI","B. Decrease calorie intake","C. Confer with dietician","D. Plan a return visit in one (1) week"],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":225,"question":"Which of the following nursing assessment findings support the diagnosis of Cushing syndrome?","options":["A. Darkening or pigmentation of the skin","B. Irritability, anxiety and depression","C. Weight gain and fatty deposits around midsection and upper back","D. New or worsened high blood pressure"],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":226,"question":"An indication for correct placement of nasogastric tube prior to feeding includes","options":["A. Aspirate small amount of mucus","B. Bubbles are seen when the tube is inserted in water","C. Client says NG tube can be felt at the back","D. The PH of the content aspirated is 3"],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":227,"question":"Which of the following is a concern for a client with partial thickness burns?","options":["A. Acute pain","B. Imbalance nutrition","C. Risk for excess fluid volume","D. Impaired tissue perfusion"],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":228,"question":"Another name for racial immunity is","options":["A. Active immunity","B. Passive immunity","C. Innate immunity","D. Acquired immunity"],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":229,"question":"Immunity conferred by toxoid administration is","options":["A. Innate immunity","B. Active immunity","C. Passive immunity","D. Herd immunity"],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":230,"question":"An example of activity carried out for primary prevention is","options":["A. Diagnosis","B. Screening","C. Chemoprophylaxis","D. Treatment"],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":231,"question":"Which of the following is not a feature of vision?","options":["A. Short","B. Succinct","C. Inspiring","D. Ambiguous"],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":232,"question":"Core value of an organization is also called","options":["A. Core motive","B. Core intent","C. Core tenet","D. Core mission"],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":233,"question":"Core value is the extent of ................ the organization is ready to maintain.","options":["A. Knowledge","B. Capacity","C. Integrity","D. Inspiration"],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":234,"question":"............is the reason for the organization's existence, a clear description of the activities of the organization","options":["A. Core mission","B. Core purpose","C. Core movement","D. Core activities"],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":235,"question":"............. is creative, looking to a future of greatness; it keeps the organization as well as individual motivated even if the founders are no longer in existence.","options":["A. Policy","B. Envision future","C. Envisioned vision","D. Future"],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":236,"question":"If vision is taken away, an organization can set into ......","options":["A. Order","B. Progress","C. Movement","D. Confusion"],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":237,"question":"Take away skills and have _____________________","options":["A. Organisational progress","B. Organisation stress","C. Organisation anxiety","D. Organisation failure"],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":238,"question":"Lack of resources can cause ................in an organization","options":["A. Slow down","B. Frustration","C. Efficiency","D. Others"],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":239,"question":"Lack of action plan can cause ......................","options":["A. Progress","B. False start","C. Clear way","D. None of the above"],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":240,"question":"An entrepreneur must be open to ....... and be ready to adjust.","options":["A. Criticism","B. Challenge","C. Other","D. None of the above"],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":241,"question":"The need for a business plan includes all except:","options":["A. Planning to launch a new business","B. Expanding your existing business","C. Adding a new product or product line","D. Increasing your labour force"],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":242,"question":"A plan must be ..................","options":["A. Readable","B. Accommodating","C. Explicit","D. Durable"],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":243,"question":"One of the benefits of planning is ..........","options":["A. It justifies your plans and actions","B. It increases \"firefight\"","C. It keeps ideas in your memory","D. It indicates your inability"],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":244,"question":"A written business plan should have all the following except ___","options":["A. Financial information","B. Product or service","C. Business objective","D. Liquidation plan"],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":245,"question":"The importance of feasibility study cannot be overemphasized as it -","options":["A. Provides comprehensive details about the business to determine if, and how it can succeed, and serve as a valuable tool for developing a good business plan","B. Does not list in details all the things you need to make the business works.","C. Does not identify logistical and other business related problems and solutions.","D. Does not serve as a solid foundation for developing your business plan."],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":246,"question":"The type of business you are planning should be stated under -","options":["A. Description of the business","B. Marketing","C. Organization","D. All of the above"],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":247,"question":"Which of the following question will be answered in a business plan under organization?","options":["A. What products or services will you sell?","B. Who are your potential customers?","C. How will you promote sales?","D. Who will manage the business?"],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":248,"question":"The following except ............. is a component of feasibility study.","options":["A. Executive summary","B. Product/Service","C. Acquisition","D. Technology"],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":249,"question":"The importance of feasibility studies include","options":["A. Listing in details all the things you need to make the business works.","B. Identifying logistical and other business related problems and solutions.","C. Serving as a solid foundation for developing your business plan.","D. All of the above"],,,"answer":"D"},
  {"id":250,"question":"The need for a full-scale business plan according to Cagan (2006) is spurred by the following except one:","options":["A. On plan to launch a new business.","B. You want to expand your existing business into new markets.","C. You want to add a new product or product line.","D. None of the above"],"answer":"D"}
]
,
  {"id":251,"question":"The term used to described the part of the limb which is farthest away from the point of attachment of the limb is","options":["A. Superior.","B. Proximal.","C. Inferior.","D. Distal."],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":252,"question":"The following are characteristics of stratified epithelial cells EXCEPT","options":["A. They generate from below.","B. They are less durable than simple epithelial.","C. Their major role is protection.","D. They are more durable than simple epithelial."],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":253,"question":"The epithelial lining of the digestive, respiratory and urinary systems, glandular cells of the liver and pancreas is formed from","options":["A. Ectoderm.","B. Mesoderm.","C. Endoderm.","D. Trophoplast."],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":254,"question":"A condition of the bone marrow in which the formed elements of the blood are simultaneously depressed is known as","options":["A. Thalassemia","B. Iron-deficiency anaemia.","C. Aplastic anaemia","D. Haemolytic anaemia."],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":255,"question":"A clinical condition characterized by massive proteinuria, hypoalbuminemia, hyperlipemia and oedema is known as","options":["A. Nephrosis.","B. Glomerulitis.","C. Nephritis.","D. Nephrotic syndrome."],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":256,"question":"Highly specialized nerve cells that generate and conduct nerve impulses are called","options":["A. Neurones.","B. Ganglion.","C. Cerebellum.","D. Pons varoli."],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":257,"question":"The part of the bone that forms the long axis of the bone is","options":["A. Epiphysis.","B. Diaphysis or shaft.","C. Membranes.","D. Epiphyseal plate."],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":258,"question":"Which part of the bone acts as a shock absorber?","options":["A. Tendon.","B. Cartilage.","C. Muscle.","D. Ligament."],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":259,"question":"The major muscles in the buttocks include:","options":["A. Rectus muscles and Rhomboid major.","B. Trapezius muscles and Teres major.","C. Gluteus medius and gluteus maximus.","D. Soleus muscles and Fibularis longus."],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":260,"question":"One of the following is NOT a characteristic of dendrite of motor neurone?","options":["A. They are short.","B. They are tapering.","C. They are diffusely branching extension.","D. They are long."],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":261,"question":"Cerebral hemispheres accounts for..........percentage of total brain mass.","options":["A. 83","B. 90","C. 73","D. 63"],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":262,"question":"The auricle and pinna constitute the........part of the ear.","options":["A. External","B. Middle","C. Internal","D. Cochlea"],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":263,"question":"One of the following is a chemical that ears its effect on the same cell that secretes them","options":["A. Paracrine.","B. Endocrines","C. Autocrines","D. Exocrine."],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":264,"question":"The hormone that influence the energy metabolism of most body cells and help to resist stressor is:","options":["A. Growth hormone","B. Thyroid hormone.","C. Adrenalin","D. Glucocorticoids."],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":265,"question":"The stomach is bounded by the following organs superiorly EXCEPT the","options":["A. Diaphragm","B. Left lobe of the liver","C. Spleen.","D. Oesophagus."],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":266,"question":"The duodenum is about.....cm long","options":["A. 35 -45","B. 25 -30","C. 55-65","D. 75 -85"],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":267,"question":"The part of the colon that runs across the front of the abdominal cavity inferior to the stomach is","options":["A. Ascending colon","B. Descending colon","C. Caecum.","D. Transverse colon"],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":268,"question":"The circumflex artery is a branch of","options":["A. Anterior descending artery","B. Left coronary artery","C. Right coronary artery","D. Descending aorta"],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":269,"question":"The following statements are TRUE about coronary arteries EXCEPT","options":["A. Circumflex artery supplies the left atrium and lateral wall of the left ventricle","B. Left anterior descending arteries supplies the anterior sall of the left ventricle","C. Right coronary artery supplies the left ventricle","D. Right coronary artery supplies the right side of the heart"],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":270,"question":"One of the following is an increase in the rate and depth of breathing that exceeds the body's need to remove Carbon dioxide (CO2)","options":["A. Hyperventilation.","B. Hypercarpnoca.","C. Hypoventilation.","D. Dyspnoea."],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":271,"question":"Which of the following therapeutic interventions uses moist heat?","options":["A. Sitz bath.","B. Aquathermus pad.","C. Heat lamp.","D. Commercial hot pack."],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":272,"question":"The following are protected by non keratinised stratified squamous epithelium EXCEPT","options":["A. Pharynx.","B. Conjunctiva.","C. Skin.","D. Vagina."],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":273,"question":"The following are natural hemostatic process EXCEPT","options":["A. Vasoconstriction.","B. Fibrolysis.","C. Platelet formation.","D. Clot formation."],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":274,"question":"A client with history of peptic ulcer disease develops a fever of 38.30C, which of the following signs strongly indicate that the client has peritonitis?","options":["A. Abdominal rigidity.","B. Hyperactive bowel sounds.","C. Abdominal pain.","D. Abdominal flexibility."],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":275,"question":"Which of the following explains the influence of aging on the development of peripheral vascular disease","options":["A. Increased viscosity of blood.","B. Increased peripheral resistance.","C. Decreased peripheral resistance.","D. Decreased viscosity of blood."],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":276,"question":"The primary goal of peripheral vascular bypass surgery is to","options":["A. Prevent blood infection.","B. Relieve vascular pain.","C. Reroute blood circulation.","D. Substitute blond vessels."],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":277,"question":"To maintain adequate glomerular filtration, it is most important for the client to have adequate","options":["A. Intravascular volume and cardiac output.","B. Serum albumin and stroke volume.","C. Oncotic pressure and systemic vascular resistance.","D. Hydrostatic pressure."],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":278,"question":"The Nurse is developing a discharge home care plan for a patient with lymphoma, the Nurse should emphasize the following EXCEPT","options":["A. Avoid crowds or other large gathering.","B. Take all medications as prescribed.","C. Stop using medications when you feel alright.","D. Do not share personal toiletries."],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":279,"question":"The most appropriate nursing intervention for determining fluid balance in a client with end stage renal failure is","options":["A. Weigh patient daily.","B. Monitor urine specific gravity.","C. Monitor intake and output daily.","D. Record vital signs daily."],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":280,"question":"The first stage of a stress response is","options":["A. Stage of resistance.","B. Stage of alarm reaction.","C. Stage of exhaustion.","D. Stage of flight."],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":281,"question":"The following are symptoms of severe hypernatremia EXCEPT","options":["A. Disorientation.","B. Hallucination.","C. Irritability.","D. Thirst."],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":282,"question":"A client with recurrent urolithiasis should be restricted from taking one of the following minerals","options":["A. Calcium.","B. Sodium.","C. Phosphorus.","D. Magnesium."],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":283,"question":"Which of the following is NOT a phase in the cell cycle?","options":["A. GI (Gap One) phase.","B. S (Synthesis) phase.","C. G2 (Gap two) phase.","D. Protein phase (P)."],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":284,"question":"The pain associated with acute pancreatitis is characterized by","options":["A. Lower abdominal pain radiating to hip.","B. Pain around the stomach radiating to the back.","C. Lower abdominal pain radiating to the groin.","D. Abdominal pain radiating to lower and middle abdomen."],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":285,"question":"A client is admitted with mitral valve disease and left ventricular dysfunction. What is the most reliable test to determine the cardiac status?","options":["A. Cardiac catherization.","B. Echocardiogram.","C. Electrocardiogram.","D. Stress test."],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":286,"question":"The primary reason for performing coronary artery bypass surgery is to:","options":["A. Reduce overall contractility of the heart muscles.","B. Increase oxygen supply to the heart muscles.","C. Decrease oxygen overload to the cardiac muscles.","D. Reduce plague formation in the carotid artery."],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":287,"question":"A client on nitroglycerine treatment complained of throbbing headache, the Nurse should","options":["A. Administer prescribed analgesics.","B. Stop nitroglycerine treatment.","C. Give nitroglycerine with few glasses of water.","D. Position patient in supine position to alleviate the headache."],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":288,"question":"A hypertensive client on Frusemide, Atenolol and Ramipril developed a second degree heart block (Mobitz type 1). Which of the following actions should the Nurse take?","options":["A. Prepare for cardioversion.","B. Withhold the atenolol.","C. Set up for arterial line.","D. Withhold Ramipril."],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":289,"question":"The most common cause of dementia in the general population is","options":["A. Parkinson disease.","B. Vascular disease.","C. Alzheimer's disease.","D. Epilepsy."],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":290,"question":"Parkinson's disease is caused by the degeneration of Neurones in an aea of the brain called","options":["A. Basal ganglia.","B. Cerebellum.","C. Corpus callosum.","D. Substantia nigra."],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":291,"question":"Damage to the glomerulus leads to","options":["A. Increase permeability of the glomerular membrane.","B. Decrease permeability of the glomerular membrane.","C. Cessation of permeability of the glomerular membrane.","D. Destruction of permeability of the membrane."],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":292,"question":"Categories of self-care requisites according to Orem's theory of Nursing include all EXCEPT","options":["A. Developmental.","B. Fundamental.","C. Universal.","D. Health deviation."],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":293,"question":"The Nurse is providing pre-operative care for a booked cardiac surgery patient. The most import action during this period is?","options":["A. Discuss with the client the steps of myocardial cellular metabolism.","B. provide pre-operative education regarding the mechanics of the cardio pulmonary by-pass machine","C. Perform a thorough nursing assessment to provide an accurate baseline for post-operative evaluation.","D. Discuss with the client and family the anticipated amount of post-operative chest tube chest drainage"],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":294,"question":"A reduction in one of the following laboratory measurements will provide an indication that treatment is successful in the treatment of Cushing's syndrome","options":["A. Serum glucose levels.","B. Urine sodium levels.","C. Serum potassium levels.","D. Gastric pH."],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":295,"question":"A patient with angina pectoris was instructed NOT to swallow glyceryl trinitrate tablet but place it under the tongue because","options":["A. It cannot be absorbed by the gastro intestinal mucosa.","B. It has high metabolic effect.","C. It is bitter and can cause vomiting","D. It can cause severe diarrhoea."],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":296,"question":"Bronchial asthmatic attack that is triggered by foreign allergies is classified as","options":["A. Atopic asthma","B. Non-atopic asthma.","C. Cardiac asthma","D. Foreign allergic asthma"],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":297,"question":"The constant process of adding or deleting elements within a culture is called","options":["A. Culture shock","B. Cultural relativism.","C. Culture change.","D. Cultural dynamism."],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":298,"question":"The presence of multiple illnesses simultaneously in a person is called","options":["A. Comorbidity.","B. Co-existence.","C. Compromise.","D. Comortality."],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":299,"question":"A group of persons having a defined membership and specified purpose is known as","options":["A. Informal group.","B. Coherent group","C. Formal group","D. Incoherent group"],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":300,"question":"A field of study that explores the biopsychosocial issues of aging is known as","options":["A. Gynecology.","B. Geriatoiogy","C. Gerontology","D. Geratonlogy."],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":301,"question":"Presence of contradictory and often competing role expectations is otherwise referred to as","options":["A. Role behaviour.","B. Role ambiguity.","C. Role conflict.","D. Role overload."],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":302,"question":"Which of the following techniques is used in assessing crepitations in patients with Osteoarihrius of the knees","options":["A. Percussion.","B. Palpation.","C. Inspection.","D. Auscultation."],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":303,"question":"A client in balanced suspension traction for a fractured femur needs to be positioned towards the head of the bed. During repositioning, the Nurse should","options":["A. Release the weight and replace immediately after positioning.","B. Lift the traction and the client during repositioning.","C. Place slightly additional tension on the traction cot.","D. Maintain the same degree of traction and tension."],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":304,"question":"The following are clinical features of Osteoarthritis EXCEPT","options":["A. Crepitation's.","B. Joint stiffness.","C. Joint trauma.","D. Pain that relieves by resting the joint."],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":305,"question":"Which of the following is the most obvious clinical manifestation of dislocation?","options":["A. Painful bone.","B. Swelling of the soft tissue surrounding the joints.","C. Asymmetry of the musculoskeletal contour.","D. Tenderness."],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":306,"question":"Which of the following is a chronic inflammatory disease that primarily affect the sacroiliac joint, apophysical and costovertebral joints of the spine and adjacent soft tissues?","options":["A. Osteomyelitis.","B. Arthritis.","C. Ankylosing spondylitis.","D. Lyme's disease."],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":307,"question":"One of these will be the appropriate thing to do if you are trapped in a burming building","options":["A. Go into a room with window and shut the door.","B. If you have to cross a smoke-filled room, stay upright.","C. If you have to escape through a window, go out hands first.","D. Lower yourself to the full length of your legs before dropping down."],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":308,"question":"The most common cause of shock is","options":["A. Fear.","B. Severe blood loss.","C. Stress.","D. Diarrhoea."],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":309,"question":"One of these is NOT a priority in the emergency treatment of severe burns?","options":["A. Treatment of pain.","B. Rapid cooling of the burn.","C. Ensuring breathing.","D. Ensuring patient is not in shock."],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":310,"question":"In a case of bleeding varicose vein, the following should be done EXCEPT","options":["A. Assist the casualty to lie down on her back with the legs at the same level.","B. Apply firm, direct pressure on the area using sterile dressing.","C. Remove garments like elastic-topped stocking.","D. Monitor and record vital signs."],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":311,"question":"Strains and sprains should initially be treated using the following EXCEPT","options":["A. Rest the injured part.","B. Apply warm compress.","C. Compress the injury.","D. Elevate the injured part."],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":312,"question":"One of these should not be part of care during asthmatic attack?","options":["A. Encourage client to keep calm.","B. Get client to take a puff of her inhaler.","C. Encourage client to lie down.","D. Ask client to breathe slowly and deeply."],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":313,"question":"To provide First Aid to a conscious spinal injury casualty, the first aider should do the following EXCEPT","options":["A. Reassure the casualty and advise her not to move.","B. Kneel behind the casualty, steady and support the head in a lateral position.","C. Continue to support the casualty's head until emergency medical services take over.","D. Get help to monitor and record the vital signs."],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":314,"question":"Emergency treatment for fractured collar bone include the following EXCEPT","options":["A. Help the casualty to sit down.","B. Lay the affected arm transversely across her chest.","C. Ask her to support the elbow with her other hand,","D. Secure the arm to the chest with a broad fold bandage."],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":315,"question":"The presence of calculi in the gall bladder is called","options":["A. Cholecystitis.","B. Cholelithiasis.","C. Cholesatoma.","D. Chondrolysis."],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":316,"question":"Which of the following represents a condition characterized by the absence of spermatozoa in he semen?","options":["A. Oligospermia.","B. Polyspermia.","C. Azoospermia.","D. Asthenospermia."],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":317,"question":"Antrum is a cavity found in the","options":["A. Uteus,","B. Graffian follicles,","C. Ovaries,","D. Fallopian tubes."],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":318,"question":"Which of the following are examples of paraphilias?","options":["A. Transvestism, voyeurism, organismic disorders.","B. Sexual masochism, transvestism, voyeurism.","C. Pedophilia, exhibitionism, organismic disorders.","D. Dyspareunia, vaginismus, sexual sadism."],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":319,"question":"Amniocentesis refers to………………………………….","options":["A. A diagnostic procedure of withdrawing a small amount of amniotic fluid from the amniotic sac.","B. Collection of fluid in the fallopian tube of pregnant woman.","C. Withdrawal of allatonic fluid from pregnant womarn.","D. Chemical analysis of fluid from pregnant woman."],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":320,"question":"The term used in describing failure of testes to descend into the scrotum 1S","options":["A. Cryptorchidism.","B. Castration.","C. Paedogenesis.","D. Impotency."],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":321,"question":"Part of the sperm involved in penetrating egg membrane is the","options":["A. Autosomes.","B. Allosomes.","C. Acrosomes.","D. Tail."],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":322,"question":"Corpus Latium develops from the","options":["A. Oocyte.","B. Neplhrostome.","C. Graafian follicle.","D. Chorionic villi."],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":323,"question":"When a couple complain of infertility, the first essential step is to:","options":["A. Take careful detailed history interviewing the man and woman separately.","B. Take careful history interviewing the man and woman together.","C. Request for sperm specimen for sperm count.","D. Order for hystero-salphingography."],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":324,"question":"The basic functional unit of a matured placenta is the","options":["A. Syncitium.","B. Mesoderm.","C. Chorionic villi.","D. Trophoplast."],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":325,"question":"Which of the following is NOT a feature of gynaecoid pelvis?","options":["A. Round brim.","B. Shallow cavity.","C. Heart shaped brim.","D. Well curved sacrum."],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":326,"question":"The most reliable test for differentiating between conductive and sensorineural deafness 1S","options":["A. Watch tick test","B. Falacies","C. Turming fork test","D. Conversational voice test"],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":327,"question":"A pedunculated mass lying in the external auditory canal refers to","options":["A. Otorhoea.","B. Aural polyp.","C. Otomycosis.","D. Myringitis."],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":328,"question":"Otorhoea is caused by all of the following EXCEPT","options":["A. Otomycosis.","B. Labyrinthitis.","C. Myelitis.","D. Myringitis."],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":329,"question":"The term used in describing a hallucination of the sense of equillibrum and movement, where the person feels that either his surroundings are going rOUnd him, or he himself is rotating is","options":["A. Tinnitus.","B. Otitis.","C. Vertigo.","D. Myringitis."],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":330,"question":"One of the following terms is used in describing acute ulceration involving one or both tonsils and spreading to the pillars, soft palate and gums","options":["A. Vincent's angina.","B. Meniere's disease.","C. Quinsy.","D. Aural Polyps."],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":331,"question":"Vitamin A deficiency can cause all of the following EXCEPT","options":["A. Night blindness.","B. Keratomalacia.","C. Dermoid.","D. Xerosis."],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":332,"question":"A. Herbert's pits are seen in","options":["A. Spring catarrh.","B. Traucoma.","C. Herpetic conjunctivitis.","D. Ophthalmia neonatorium."],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":333,"question":"Retinoblastoma is a term used in describing","options":["A. White mass behind the iris.","B. Frequent tumor in childhood.","C. Common malignant tumor of the eye found in children.","D. Chrosomal abnormalities of the retina."],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":334,"question":"Increased nervous tension, accelerated pulse. loss of body weight and increased oxygen Consuption in a child is as a result of over productiton of which of the following glands?","options":["A. Gonads.","B. Pituitary gland.","C. Pancreas.","D. Thyroid gland."],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":335,"question":"The clouding or opacity within the crystalline 1ense that leads to gradual painless blurmns eventual loss of vision is called.","options":["A. Glaucoma.","B. Cataract.","C. Traucoma.","D. Chalazion."],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":336,"question":"1he variable that are NOT under study but can create some effects on the variables that are being studied are referred to as","options":["A. Extraneous variables.","B. Dependent variables.","C. Independent variables.","D. Stimulus variables."],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":337,"question":"Research implies all of the following EXCEPT","options":["A. Systematic approach to problem solving.","B. An empirical investigation.","C. A scientific approach to problem solving.","D. Systematic assessment of problem."],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":338,"question":"Descriptive statistics are used for the purpose of","options":["A. Estimating population parameters and making deductions.","B. Predicting the population characteristics and making inferences about them.","C. Describing the data in relation to sample of study.","D. Explaining relationships established in hypothesis."],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":339,"question":"The level of consistency, stability and dependability of a measuring instrument refer to its","options":["A. Validity.","B. Usability.","C. Applicability.","D. Reliability."],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":340,"question":"The synopsis of research report that gives the reader a clear and precise idea of the entire work is the","options":["A. Summary.","B. Recommendation.","C. Abstract.","D. Proposal."],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":341,"question":"When data collected are arranged in any order it is called","options":["A. Raw data","B. An array of data","C. Data set","D. Data arrangement."],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":342,"question":"The following represent data collection instruments EXCEKT","options":["A. Interview.","B. Observation.","C. Hypothesis.","D. Questionnaire."],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":343,"question":"Case control study is also known 20","options":["A. Prospective study","B. Retrospective study.","C. Incidence study","D. Cohort study"],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":344,"question":"A graphical representation of data that explains correlation between variables is known a","options":["A. Histogram","B. Scattergram","C. Frequency polygon.","D. Bar chart"],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":345,"question":"The steps in data processing is in the following ordes","options":["A. Preparation, tabulation, presentation and analysis.","B. Analysis, presentation, tabulation and preparation.","C. Tabulation, preparation, presentation and analysis.","D. Presentation, preparation, tabulation and analysis."],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":346,"question":"The following are types of neuroses EXCEPT","options":["A. Anxiety.","B. Hysteria","C. Dementia","D. Depression."],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":347,"question":"Which is the connonest type of hallucination in oanic poychoses?","options":["A. Visual,","B. Auditory.","C. Tactile.","D. Gustatory."],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":348,"question":"Rapid conversation with logically unconnected shifting of topics is called","options":["A. Irritability.","B. Anxiety.","C. Flight of ideas.","D. Ecstasy."],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":349,"question":"The type of somatoform disorder characterised by morbid preoccupation with one's body a partial withdrawal of interest from the environment is","options":["A. Phobia.","B. Hypochondriasis.","C. Obsessive/compulsive.","D. Schizophrenia."],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":350,"question":"Succinylcholine (Anectine) chloride is often used before electro-convulsive treatment in order","options":["A. Produce a short-acting anaesthesia.","B. Reduce tracheobronchial secretions.","C. Decrease the intensity of tonic-clonic contractions.","D. Prevent respiratory distress."],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":351,"question":"The nurse manager presided over a meeting on how to improve staff performance. Which of these statements by a junior nurse demonstrates more need for teaching?","options":["A. Management is all about inspiring others","B. Management is a function of administrators","C. Management is about achieving set goals","D. Management is a process"],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":352,"question":"The Nurse Manager carried out a process that involves setting organisational goals and deciding in advance how to achieve them, when to achieve them. She is said to be doing","options":["A. Management","B. Organizing","C. Directing","D. Planning"],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":353,"question":"The process of identifying the task to be done, who will do the task and when it is to be done is referred to as","options":["A. Management","B. Organizing","C. Directing","D. Planning"],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":354,"question":"As a unit head, Nurse Alice is concerned about having large number of staff but performing below average and doing least work possible. The phenomenon she observed is termed","options":["A. Systematic wandering","B. Coordinated soldering","C. Systematic soldering","D. System management"],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":355,"question":"Which of the following is not a characteristic of strategic planning?","options":["A. Long-term goal-setting.","B. Extends to 3-5 years in the future.","C. Focuses on routine tasks.","D. Determines directions of the organization."],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":356,"question":"You are asked by your instructor to discuss about Contingency Theory. What should you include in your discussion?","options":["A. It is a theory in leadership that views the pattern of leader behavior as dependent on the interaction of the personality and the needs of the situation.","B. It considers that leaders must provide followers a sense of security and approval and discipline to be successful in an output.","C. It emphasizes that both leaders and followers should act on one another to raise their motivation.","D. It states that leadership qualities inspire followers to be motivated in what they do."],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":357,"question":"Which statement describes an informal leader?","options":["A. Anna who is appointed because of her competencies and continuing education","B. Maria who becomes the leader of the team because of her years of experience in the department","C. Eduard who is considered the leader of the team since he was given the legitimate authority to act as one.","D. Alexandra who is chosen by the administration because of her age and knowledge in the area of work."],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":358,"question":"Why is good communication important in managing personnel?","options":["A. It motivates personnel to do their jobs well","B. It promotes independence and collaboration","C. It fosters influence and power","D. All of the above"],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":359,"question":"Downward communication is described as?","options":["A. The communication is between two supervisors","B. The flow of communication is from the head nurse to the supervisor","C. The flow of communication is from the chief nurse to the head nurse","D. The flow of communication is from the staff nurse to the chief nurse"],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":360,"question":"Henry is a Unit Manager I the Medical Unit. He is not satisfied with the way things are going in his unit. The patient satisfaction rate is 60% for two consecutive months and staff morale is at its lowest. Which of the following actions is a priority for Henry?","options":["A. Call for a staff meeting and take this up in the agenda.","B. Seek help from her manager.","C. Develop a strategic action on how to deal with these concerns.","D. Ignore the issues since these will be resolved naturally."],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":361,"question":"Nurse Stephanie delegates effectively if she has authority to act, which is best defined as:","options":["A. Having a responsibility to direct others.","B. Being accountable to the organization.","C. Having a legitimate right to act.","D. Telling others what to do."],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":362,"question":"What are the tasks that should not be delegated to a non-professional staff?","options":["A. Doing the vital signs","B. Turning the client every two hours","C. Grooming and bathing the client","D. Assessment of neurological deficits"],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":363,"question":"Ms. Caputo notices that the Chief Nurse Executive has charismatic leadership style. Which of the following behaviors best describes this style?","options":["A. Possesses inspirational quality that makes followers gets attracted of him and regards him with reverence","B. Acts as he does because he expects that his behavior will yield positive results","C. Uses visioning as the core of his leadership","D. Matches his leadership style to the situation at hand"],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":364,"question":"Which of the following does not characterize a transactional leader?","options":["A. Focuses on management tasks","B. Is a caretaker","C. Uses trade-offs to meet goals","D. Inspires others with vision"],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":365,"question":"Leadership theory which states that \"leaders are born and not made,\" refers to which of the following theories?","options":["A. Trait","B. Charismatic","C. Great Man","D. Situational"],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":366,"question":"The principle which provided for all the employees to follow orders and instructions from one person and not from anyone else refers to?","options":["A. Scalar chain","B. Discipline","C. Unity of command","D. Order"],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":367,"question":"The principle that gives emphasis on a team to put their efforts together towards the attainment of the goals refers to?","options":["A. Span of control","B. Unity of direction","C. Unity of command","D. Command responsibility"],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":368,"question":"Which of the following statements regarding conflict is not true?","options":["A. Can be destructive if the level is too high.","B. Is not beneficial; hence it should be prevented at all times.","C. May result in poor performance.","D. May create leaders."],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":369,"question":"Nurse Manager Katherine will shun discussing conflict until she \"Buys time\". Which of the following conflict resolution strategies she uses?","options":["A. Smoothing","B. Compromise","C. Avoidance","D. Restriction"],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":370,"question":"What type of conflict refers to when there are two or more opposing incompatible demands that arise and priority differences affect the resolution of the conflict.","options":["A. Interpersonal conflict","B. Organizational conflict","C. Intrapersonal conflict","D. Answers A & B"],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":371,"question":"Even with its complexity, Nervous system is among the first systems to develop; thus, its development begins at:","options":["A. Fourth week of gestation","B. Fifth week of gestation","C. Second week of gestation","D. Third week of gestation"],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":372,"question":"All the body structures originate from germ layers, specifically the Nervous system originates from;","options":["A. Endoderm","B. Mesoderm","C. Ectoderm","D. Primitive streak"],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":373,"question":"The fluid-filled internal cavity of the neural tube is called","options":["A. Neurocoele","B. Ventricles","C. Neural crest","D. Neural fold"],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":374,"question":"The raised edges of the neural plate increased in height and meet to form a neural tube. The edges of the neural plates are therefore called:","options":["A. Neurolation","B. Neural fold","C. Neural crest","D. Neurocoele"],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":375,"question":"The expansion of the anterior part of the neural tube produces;","options":["A. Primary brain vesicles","B. Secondary brain vesicles","C. Prosencephalon","D. All of the above"],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":376,"question":"The fluid – filled internal cavity of the neural tube develops to form;","options":["A. Neuroglia","B. Spinal cord","C. Ventricles","D. Meninges"],"answer":"C"},
  {"id":377,"question":"The Metencephalon which is one of the secondary brain vesicles develops to form the following structures except;","options":["A. Medulla","B. Cerebellum","C. Pons","D. Upper fourth ventricle"],"answer":"A"},
