  {"id":379,"question":"For convenience, Nervous system can be classified in to Central and Peripheral Nervous system. the Central Nervous System performs the following except;","options":["A. Integrating","B. Processing","C. Coordinating","D. Detecting"],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":380,"question":"As one of their characteristics, neurons are considered amitotic because of;","options":["A. Large number of mitochondria","B. Presence of myelin sheath","C. Absence of Nissl bodies","D. Absence of centriole"],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":381,"question":"The Sensory receptors that detect body movement and position are called;","options":["A. Nociceptors","B. Proprioceptors","C. Mechanoceptors","D. Baroreceptors"],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":382,"question":"Dendrites play key roles in intercellular communication, they conduct nerve impulses toward the cell body. Thus, the less dendrites a neuron has, the more nerve impulses a neuron can receive.","options":["A. True","B. False","C. none of the above","D. All of the above"],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":383,"question":"A group of neuron cell bodies in the CNS with a common function is called","options":["A. Nucleus","B. Center","C. Gray matter","D. Cortex"],"answer":"A"},
  {"id":384,"question":"The visceral sensory components transmit nerve impulses from blood vessels and viscera to the CNS. They include sense of","options":["A. Pain and touch","B. Pain and strecth","C. temperature and stretch","D. none of the above"],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":385,"question":"Neuron is considered amitotic because it….","options":["A. Has large number of mitochondria","B. Lacks Ribosome","C. Loses Nucleus","D. Lacks centromere"],"answer":"D"},
