  {"id":497,"question":"What happens in statistics when t-value is greater than critical/table value?","options":["A. Null hypothesis is accepted","B. Null hypothesis is rejected","C. Alternative hypothesis is rejected","D. Alternative hyperthesis is accepted"],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":498,"question":"The following are crises intervention strategies for helping a family deal with sudden death in the emergency department EXCEPT","options":["A. Take the family to a private place","B. Do not allow the family to talk about the deceased and what he or she meant to them","C. Avoid divulging unnecessary information","D. Avoid giving sedation to family members"],"answer":"B"},
  {"id":499,"question":"The following are causes of tsunami EXCEPT","options":["A. Explosive volcanic eruptions in the sea or oceans","B. Sudden vertical movement of the earth","C. Convergence of destructive plates in the oceans floor","D. Sudden horizontal movement of the earth"],"answer":"D"},
  {"id":500,"question":"A 45-year-old man presents with severe chest pain radiating to the left arm, diaphoresis, and shortness of breath. What is the priority nursing action?","options":["A. Administer sublingual nitroglycerin","B. Obtain a 12-lead ECG","C. Administer aspirin 300mg chewed","D. Start oxygen at 4L/min via nasal cannula"],"answer":"C"}
